WEBVTT

00:41.416 --> 00:43.961
NO TAIL TO TELL

00:44.044 --> 00:46.171
SEOUL SANGSEO POLICE STATION

00:52.010 --> 00:53.053
Damn it.

00:58.559 --> 01:00.143
Mr. Kang, you can step out now.

01:08.193 --> 01:09.820
You just keep outdoing yourself.

01:10.487 --> 01:12.614
You're really a piece of work, aren't you?

01:17.244 --> 01:18.620
Hey, Si-yeol.

01:19.955 --> 01:21.081
What?

01:23.083 --> 01:25.752
Are you acting out
because I told you to quit soccer?

01:27.462 --> 01:28.797
No, it's not like that.

01:28.880 --> 01:31.967
Jeez, you're a total nutjob.

01:32.050 --> 01:34.595
Is apologizing to me that difficult?

01:35.887 --> 01:38.849
You've got a seriously nasty temper.

01:38.932 --> 01:40.726
Seriously.

01:44.771 --> 01:45.647
Fine.

01:46.148 --> 01:47.065
You win.

01:49.484 --> 01:51.486
Come back to training tomorrow.

01:51.570 --> 01:52.779
But on one condition.

01:53.447 --> 01:55.824
You'd better get your head in the game.

01:56.617 --> 01:57.784
Listen.

01:58.869 --> 02:02.414
Let's win the championship this season
and get promoted to the third division.

02:10.088 --> 02:11.214
Are you crazy?

02:15.552 --> 02:18.221
You expect me to play
in the fourth division?

02:19.389 --> 02:20.891
Are you out of your mind?

02:26.980 --> 02:28.565
I can't live like that.

02:29.066 --> 02:29.983
No.

02:30.734 --> 02:32.110
I won't, damn it!

02:32.903 --> 02:34.988
Seriously…

02:39.201 --> 02:41.787
Seriously, what the hell
is wrong with him?

02:54.591 --> 02:56.259
- Hey, Woo-seok.
- Si-yeol.

02:56.343 --> 02:57.302
Where are you right now?

02:57.386 --> 02:58.679
Are you in London too?

02:58.762 --> 03:00.931
Actually, Woo-seok…

03:02.265 --> 03:03.684
- The thing is--
- No, wait.

03:03.767 --> 03:06.645
Let's just meet up.

03:07.229 --> 03:08.814
Let's talk in person.

03:11.108 --> 03:12.192
I think

03:13.110 --> 03:14.820
I've become a Premier League player.

03:14.903 --> 03:17.406
That's the thing, Woo-seok--

03:17.489 --> 03:20.325
It's all thanks to you, Si-yeol.

03:22.119 --> 03:23.078
Hey, Woo-seok.

03:24.663 --> 03:25.789
The thing is,

03:26.790 --> 03:29.126
our fates have been switched.

03:31.253 --> 03:34.339
What do you mean, switched?

03:34.423 --> 03:37.843
You became
a Premier League player instead of me.

03:37.926 --> 03:42.055
And I'm playing
in the fourth division instead of you.

03:48.478 --> 03:49.980
Woo-seok?

03:53.400 --> 03:54.776
So what do we do now?

03:56.236 --> 03:57.446
What happens now?

03:58.238 --> 03:59.823
Well, I asked.

04:00.407 --> 04:02.743
She says you have to wish

04:03.285 --> 04:05.829
to have our fates switched back.

04:06.455 --> 04:07.956
A wish?

04:08.957 --> 04:10.542
I have to make a wish?

04:10.625 --> 04:15.297
Yes, because I don't have
anything left to pay for a wish.

04:17.048 --> 04:18.592
I see.

04:18.675 --> 04:21.428
Can you check your pockets or your bag?

04:21.511 --> 04:23.930
Her business card
should be in there somewhere.

04:24.014 --> 04:25.682
Woo-seok, come out here for a minute.

04:25.766 --> 04:27.350
Just a second.

04:32.856 --> 04:35.776
Si-yeol, hang on. I'll call you back.

04:35.859 --> 04:37.611
Woo-seok? Hello?

04:37.694 --> 04:38.820
Woo-seok, wait--

04:58.590 --> 05:01.635
Woo-seok, do you have any idea
how crazy things are right now?

05:01.718 --> 05:04.846
The clubs are fighting over
who's going to sign you,

05:04.930 --> 05:06.598
and the reporters keep calling.

05:06.681 --> 05:10.310
God, having such a perfect son
is exhausting!

05:13.438 --> 05:17.943
Okay, today's the day.
Let's lock in your team!

05:18.026 --> 05:20.529
And when your transfer fee comes through,

05:20.612 --> 05:22.155
can I get…

05:23.281 --> 05:24.616
a new car?

05:28.495 --> 05:30.622
- Dad--
- I know.

05:30.705 --> 05:34.334
I know we have plenty of cars, but…

05:35.293 --> 05:36.336
Dad.

05:38.755 --> 05:40.006
You're happy, right?

05:41.174 --> 05:42.425
What?

05:43.677 --> 05:45.262
Of course I am.

05:45.345 --> 05:48.598
Thanks to you, I've got it pretty good.

05:48.682 --> 05:50.100
Of course I'm happy.

05:52.561 --> 05:55.939
I really was hoping for that one car.

06:12.539 --> 06:15.876
Hello? Hey, Woo-seok.
Did you find the business card?

06:17.335 --> 06:19.588
Well, the thing is…

06:20.255 --> 06:21.673
What, it's not there?

06:23.466 --> 06:24.759
No, that's not it.

06:25.302 --> 06:26.803
Then what is it?

06:28.722 --> 06:30.765
Do we really
have to switch back right now?

06:31.933 --> 06:34.561
What… do you mean?

06:34.644 --> 06:37.355
Just one month.
Let's switch back in a month.

06:37.439 --> 06:39.941
I promise I'll switch us back then.

06:40.775 --> 06:42.861
- Hey!
- If we're switching back anyway,

06:43.528 --> 06:45.822
does it matter when we do it?

06:46.448 --> 06:48.283
Of course it does.

06:49.075 --> 06:51.828
Just give me a little more time.

06:53.163 --> 06:55.415
Hey, Woo-seok.

06:55.999 --> 06:57.792
You can't do this. Please.

06:57.876 --> 06:58.835
I'm sorry.

06:58.919 --> 07:00.795
Woo-seok!

07:00.879 --> 07:04.257
Hyeon Woo-seok! Oh, come on!

07:05.091 --> 07:07.177
I'm screwed!

07:07.260 --> 07:09.387
I'm seriously screwed!

07:10.347 --> 07:11.431
Damn it!

07:32.619 --> 07:33.620
Damn.

07:47.968 --> 07:49.844
REPUBLIC OF KOREA PASSPORT
KANG SI-YEOL

07:56.309 --> 07:58.436
- Have a nice day.
- Thank you.

08:01.982 --> 08:04.401
One ticket to London, please.
The earliest available.

08:04.484 --> 08:06.903
- Would you like a round-trip ticket?
- No, one-way.

08:09.447 --> 08:11.324
Excuse me.

08:11.408 --> 08:13.994
It looks like your passport has expired.

08:14.077 --> 08:14.953
What?

08:16.121 --> 08:17.247
Then what do I do?

08:17.872 --> 08:19.749
I have to get to London right now.

08:19.833 --> 08:22.335
And here I thought
your friendship was special.

08:22.419 --> 08:23.878
Not so special after all.

08:24.754 --> 08:25.964
You!

08:28.591 --> 08:30.135
Have you learned your lesson?

08:30.218 --> 08:32.554
I'm not really fond of stupid humans.

08:32.637 --> 08:35.432
Learned what lesson, exactly?

08:35.932 --> 08:37.934
You think I'm the one who needs a lesson?

08:38.018 --> 08:39.644
Apparently not.

08:39.728 --> 08:41.187
Wait!

08:41.271 --> 08:43.356
I seriously can't live like this.

08:43.440 --> 08:45.984
Put me back!

08:47.861 --> 08:48.737
Please.

08:54.534 --> 08:57.120
You shouldn't have been
so cocky in the first place.

08:58.329 --> 09:01.791
Well, that should do it.
I guess I've tamed you enough.

09:01.875 --> 09:03.460
Shall we end this here?

09:04.961 --> 09:07.797
When you wake up tomorrow,
everything will be back to normal.

09:09.299 --> 09:10.633
- Really?
- Yes.

09:10.717 --> 09:12.635
If you ever make a wish,

09:13.261 --> 09:17.265
always remember what happened today.

09:17.891 --> 09:20.727
So you don't make the same mistake
with me ever again.

09:22.479 --> 09:26.024
And from now on,
don't be so quick to trust people.

09:26.107 --> 09:28.401
Consider it a free lesson from me.

09:36.659 --> 09:38.620
Man…

09:40.080 --> 09:41.998
Seriously.

09:45.376 --> 09:47.670
I'll never make a wish again.

09:48.338 --> 09:50.757
Not even if my life depends on it.

09:50.840 --> 09:52.175
Never, damn it.

10:11.945 --> 10:13.113
Sorry.

10:24.415 --> 10:25.291
What?

10:28.545 --> 10:29.546
What was that?

10:40.140 --> 10:41.266
Where to?

10:53.403 --> 10:56.406
I'm sorry. I thought this was a taxi.

10:57.073 --> 10:58.741
You're right. It is a taxi.

10:58.825 --> 11:00.410
But…

11:00.493 --> 11:02.203
VACANT

11:05.540 --> 11:06.833
Sir.

11:09.878 --> 11:12.630
I'll take you exactly
where you need to be.

11:25.560 --> 11:29.063
EPISODE 4
THE PRICE OF GOOD DEEDS

11:50.210 --> 11:51.461
Who are you people?

12:25.370 --> 12:27.664
What's with the weather all of a sudden?

12:27.747 --> 12:29.332
Something feels wrong.

12:33.461 --> 12:34.921
Stay still.

12:36.214 --> 12:37.507
Who the hell are you people?

12:38.216 --> 12:40.093
What are you doing?

12:44.847 --> 12:46.099
It's not here.

12:46.182 --> 12:48.101
That's impossible. Look again.

12:52.021 --> 12:54.732
Look for yourself then. It's not here.

12:54.816 --> 12:56.943
You've got the wrong person.

12:57.026 --> 12:59.112
I have jack squat right now.

12:59.195 --> 13:02.031
I won't call the police,
so just let me go.

13:03.449 --> 13:04.701
Shut up.

13:08.037 --> 13:11.040
There's no business card
or anything remotely like it.

13:11.666 --> 13:13.418
Are you sure this is the right guy?

13:24.304 --> 13:26.472
I'll get straight to the point.

13:26.556 --> 13:28.016
We're looking for something.

13:28.975 --> 13:31.686
Hand it over,
and I promise nothing will happen to you.

13:34.230 --> 13:37.108
You have the wish-granting
business card, don't you?

13:38.026 --> 13:39.110
A business card?

13:39.193 --> 13:40.403
That's right.

13:40.486 --> 13:42.530
I have some business with that fox.

13:44.907 --> 13:46.993
Unbelievable.

13:50.371 --> 13:52.832
You did all this just for that?

13:52.915 --> 13:55.710
Kidnapping an innocent guy
and tying him up?

13:57.253 --> 13:58.296
Fine, I get it.

13:59.422 --> 14:01.215
Just untie me first.

14:01.299 --> 14:02.925
I'll just summon her for you.

14:03.009 --> 14:04.635
You think this is a joke?

14:04.719 --> 14:05.928
Hold it!

14:11.851 --> 14:13.311
What did you just say?

14:14.520 --> 14:18.649
You don't even have the card.
How are you going to summon her?

14:23.446 --> 14:26.407
Dad, should we go look at some watches?

14:27.408 --> 14:29.994
No, I'm good.
Let's find something for you instead.

14:30.078 --> 14:31.996
You've already bought me plenty today.

14:33.873 --> 14:36.250
Who knows when we'll have
a day like this again?

14:37.043 --> 14:38.711
I really want to buy you one.

14:38.795 --> 14:40.713
It's not like this is our only chance.

14:42.131 --> 14:46.386
But I wonder if they still have
that limited edition.

14:46.469 --> 14:48.096
- Let's go look.
- Shall we?

14:48.721 --> 14:49.847
Hold on.

14:51.015 --> 14:52.475
SI-YEOL

14:58.856 --> 15:01.150
Who is it? Why didn't you pick up?

15:01.234 --> 15:03.903
It's okay. I don't need to take that call.

15:03.986 --> 15:04.987
Let's hurry.

15:05.071 --> 15:07.198
We should go check out some cars later.

15:07.281 --> 15:08.324
Really?

15:08.408 --> 15:10.743
But that can wait
until the transfer talks are--

15:10.827 --> 15:12.203
You said you wanted one.

15:12.286 --> 15:14.831
Why wait? Let's buy it now.

15:14.914 --> 15:16.791
Okay, then. Let's go.

15:20.211 --> 15:23.798
Why isn't he picking up?

15:27.385 --> 15:30.638
Just wait.
I'll get her here for sure, okay?

15:36.436 --> 15:39.355
By the way, I don't know
what wish you're trying to make,

15:39.439 --> 15:41.524
but you may want
to think it through one more time.

15:41.607 --> 15:43.985
Thanks to that crazy fox…

15:45.778 --> 15:50.116
Anyhow, wishes don't work
the way you think they do.

15:50.825 --> 15:51.826
I know.

15:52.827 --> 15:54.328
I'm not going to make a wish.

15:55.455 --> 15:58.040
Then why are you
looking for the nine-tailed fox?

15:58.624 --> 15:59.750
We're going to kill her.

16:01.919 --> 16:03.546
You're going to kill her?

16:04.589 --> 16:06.466
It's not for a wish?

16:14.223 --> 16:15.224
Hey!

16:17.143 --> 16:18.436
Hello?

16:20.563 --> 16:21.564
Hey, Woo-seok.

16:24.817 --> 16:28.529
Look, I'm a bit busy right now,
so I missed your call.

16:30.490 --> 16:32.200
Okay…

16:34.702 --> 16:35.703
Si-yeol.

16:36.787 --> 16:38.039
I'm begging you, please.

16:39.540 --> 16:40.875
I just need a month.

16:41.626 --> 16:42.835
That's all I'm asking.

16:44.253 --> 16:47.757
We're going to kill her.

16:48.549 --> 16:49.550
Si-yeol?

16:51.260 --> 16:53.137
Look, Woo-seok.

16:54.305 --> 16:55.890
Let me call you back.

16:59.060 --> 17:00.102
What are you doing?

17:04.273 --> 17:05.525
I don't think this'll work.

17:07.026 --> 17:10.530
Look, I don't like
that nine-tailed fox either.

17:10.613 --> 17:14.617
But still, you don't have to kill her.

17:15.743 --> 17:16.744
Fine.

17:17.954 --> 17:20.206
If that's how you feel, then so be it.

17:20.915 --> 17:23.626
We'll just have to find another way.

18:13.426 --> 18:14.510
What is this?

18:41.662 --> 18:44.874
I'm about to lose a huge chunk
of my spiritual power again.

19:01.349 --> 19:04.018
I was wondering what was going on with me.

19:04.644 --> 19:06.145
I should've known it was you.

19:09.398 --> 19:10.399
Wait.

19:13.361 --> 19:14.570
What is all this?

19:15.279 --> 19:18.699
Look at you, crawling in here
not knowing this is where you'll die.

19:24.455 --> 19:27.041
I recognize that face.

19:33.005 --> 19:34.632
And you're that male shaman!

19:35.341 --> 19:37.927
Your name…

19:38.010 --> 19:40.221
was it Jang Do-cheol?

19:41.222 --> 19:43.099
You're quite the wicked creature.

19:43.182 --> 19:45.309
How did you know my name?

19:48.104 --> 19:49.605
Oh my gosh!

19:54.694 --> 19:56.195
Did you

19:56.278 --> 19:57.905
trap me in here?

19:58.489 --> 20:00.449
I spent years researching this.

20:01.075 --> 20:03.411
You won't be able to do a thing in there.

20:03.494 --> 20:06.247
Not even a centuries-old nine-tailed fox.

20:07.623 --> 20:10.459
A human after a fox bead…

20:12.294 --> 20:14.338
There used to be a few like you.

20:16.382 --> 20:20.511
Ever wonder what happened to them?

20:28.769 --> 20:30.187
Rumor has it

20:31.021 --> 20:34.692
this dagger can cut through anything.

20:36.068 --> 20:37.987
Humans, ghosts,

20:38.612 --> 20:40.865
and even fate decreed by Heaven.

20:54.336 --> 20:55.629
How disappointing.

20:56.589 --> 20:59.842
I thought a centuries-old nine-tailed fox
would be different.

21:18.402 --> 21:20.446
Are you about to leave?

21:23.574 --> 21:27.745
The time has come, so I must.

21:29.747 --> 21:32.875
Is your long watch finally over?

21:50.768 --> 21:51.852
What?

21:55.064 --> 21:56.524
Well?

21:56.607 --> 21:58.400
Not so disappointing now, am I?

22:05.699 --> 22:06.617
That really hurts.

22:07.993 --> 22:09.078
It hurts!

22:10.913 --> 22:12.414
Now do you wonder?

22:12.498 --> 22:15.543
About what happened
to the humans who dared chase my fox bead.

22:16.335 --> 22:18.128
How on earth…

22:18.212 --> 22:19.922
It seemed like you were
digging into my past,

22:20.005 --> 22:21.507
so I did some digging on you too.

22:22.716 --> 22:25.636
Jang Do-cheol, 54 years old.

22:26.470 --> 22:27.555
And?

22:27.638 --> 22:29.932
And he's a former high-flying
fund manager.

22:30.975 --> 22:32.935
He chose his profession wisely.

22:33.853 --> 22:36.689
With his powers, he must've predicted
every stock price perfectly.

22:36.772 --> 22:39.066
And he probably mistook it
for his own talent.

22:40.067 --> 22:40.985
Anything else?

22:41.068 --> 22:44.113
Ten years ago,
he quit a perfectly stable job

22:44.780 --> 22:47.658
and has been wandering since,
with nowhere to call home.

22:48.534 --> 22:51.620
His last known address is right here.

22:53.998 --> 22:56.458
ID CERTIFICATE: JANG DO-CHEOL
YANGHEUNG-GUN, GANGWON-DO

23:09.972 --> 23:12.933
I came to see if I could find anything,

23:13.851 --> 23:15.936
but it looks like this will take a while.

23:33.120 --> 23:34.788
If you have something to say, go ahead.

23:34.872 --> 23:36.582
I'm listening.

23:40.377 --> 23:42.212
What are you going to do with me?

23:43.797 --> 23:44.798
I'm not sure.

23:45.841 --> 23:47.176
Nothing at all, actually.

23:48.177 --> 23:51.221
- What?
- You don't have long to live anyway.

23:51.722 --> 23:52.848
You know that already.

23:53.515 --> 23:56.685
You're destined
for a particularly miserable death.

23:57.478 --> 24:00.397
So why should I bother
getting my hands dirty?

24:06.445 --> 24:07.863
And as for you.

24:07.947 --> 24:10.074
I'll be coming for you soon

24:10.741 --> 24:13.327
since you clearly
haven't learned your lesson.

24:14.578 --> 24:15.537
No!

24:15.621 --> 24:19.625
This wasn't even my idea.

24:20.167 --> 24:22.169
That guy made me do all of this.

24:35.307 --> 24:38.185
I once heard someone say…

24:39.561 --> 24:41.271
Damn it!

24:41.814 --> 24:43.107
What is it now?

24:49.196 --> 24:50.197
You…

25:08.382 --> 25:11.343
…"Heaven's net is vast and wide,

25:11.969 --> 25:14.221
yet nothing slips through."

25:22.104 --> 25:23.313
What a joke.

25:24.106 --> 25:26.191
Deities have no interest in humans.

25:27.234 --> 25:31.196
There's no world
where the guilty are justly punished.

25:33.741 --> 25:38.203
So I just need to deceive them
enough to get by as well.

25:38.787 --> 25:40.456
Get up, Kang Si-yeol.

25:41.665 --> 25:45.878
It'll be quite inconvenient for me
if you die like this.

26:10.402 --> 26:13.697
If you're going to die, do it tomorrow.
Don't make it my problem.

26:15.949 --> 26:18.577
If you die with your fate switched,

26:18.660 --> 26:21.455
the ones above
will find out what I'm up to.

26:21.538 --> 26:23.457
And that would be

26:24.458 --> 26:26.126
extremely annoying for me.

26:27.002 --> 26:28.087
Hey,

26:28.796 --> 26:30.130
are you okay?

26:31.131 --> 26:33.050
What happened to those people?

26:34.968 --> 26:36.470
Why?

26:36.553 --> 26:37.721
Planning on getting revenge?

26:38.764 --> 26:40.057
Did you…

26:41.850 --> 26:43.102
kill them?

26:45.062 --> 26:45.938
What?

26:46.021 --> 26:47.898
You must've forgotten already.

26:47.981 --> 26:49.525
I don't kill humans.

26:51.026 --> 26:52.236
Right.

26:53.403 --> 26:57.783
Though I will pay them a visit soon
and make their lives a living hell.

26:59.159 --> 27:00.369
Anyway.

27:04.957 --> 27:06.250
I'm sorry.

27:07.543 --> 27:08.669
What?

27:10.587 --> 27:14.383
I feel like you got dragged
into this because of me.

27:19.138 --> 27:20.973
Are you just going to sit there?

27:21.515 --> 27:23.183
Get up. I'll take you home.

27:24.351 --> 27:25.727
Yeah, okay.

28:46.725 --> 28:48.101
I told you

28:48.894 --> 28:50.229
this would happen,

28:50.812 --> 28:51.855
Geum-ho.

28:53.148 --> 28:54.983
You never once came to look for me.

28:55.859 --> 28:57.611
Not when your child was sick,

28:57.694 --> 28:59.905
or even after they died.

29:01.156 --> 29:02.908
Not when your family was ruined,

29:02.991 --> 29:05.827
when your husband died,
or when you were left to starve.

29:05.911 --> 29:08.664
While you were living that miserable life,

29:10.249 --> 29:13.043
why did you never once ask me
to grant you a wish?

29:13.669 --> 29:15.754
You never gave me the chance to help you.

29:19.800 --> 29:24.930
I smell the earth on you, miss.

29:26.765 --> 29:28.642
It smells like the place

29:29.601 --> 29:32.104
where I once lived, long ago.

29:35.899 --> 29:39.319
I told you that you'd be miserable.

29:40.529 --> 29:43.323
You knew you'd forget
everything in the end

29:44.074 --> 29:47.035
and die as a lonely, withered old woman.

29:49.121 --> 29:51.415
Why did you choose to endure it all?

29:52.833 --> 29:53.875
Oh my.

29:55.460 --> 29:56.878
You're such a beauty.

29:58.297 --> 30:00.340
My, how beautiful you are.

30:05.053 --> 30:07.055
I came to say goodbye.

30:08.807 --> 30:10.434
Because you're going to die today.

30:12.769 --> 30:15.355
There was something I needed to say.

30:18.108 --> 30:20.152
I will never become human.

30:23.405 --> 30:26.116
I won't love a human as you did.

30:26.700 --> 30:29.119
I won't live in misery,
and I won't die in despair.

30:30.329 --> 30:31.747
I'll never

30:33.040 --> 30:34.916
live like you.

30:42.341 --> 30:44.509
Gosh. Ma'am!

30:44.593 --> 30:45.844
Ma'am!

30:45.927 --> 30:48.138
- Oh gosh. Ma'am!
- My goodness.

30:48.764 --> 30:50.515
- Goodness!
- Gosh.

30:50.599 --> 30:51.725
Ma'am!

30:52.642 --> 30:53.769
There she is.

30:54.394 --> 30:57.939
Good grief. This senile old woman
is always wandering back here.

30:58.023 --> 30:59.900
She can't even find her own home anymore.

30:59.983 --> 31:02.277
How does she find
this place so well every time?

31:02.361 --> 31:04.237
The sun's setting. Let's go.

31:10.994 --> 31:11.953
Ma'am.

31:15.123 --> 31:16.500
No…

31:16.583 --> 31:18.418
Oh no. Ma'am!

31:19.961 --> 31:22.881
Goodness me.

31:22.964 --> 31:25.133
Ma'am…

31:25.759 --> 31:28.053
Oh no.

31:28.136 --> 31:32.140
Oh no. Ma'am! Poor thing!

31:50.450 --> 31:51.701
Wait.

31:52.369 --> 31:53.787
Are you crying?

32:00.919 --> 32:02.087
Where am I?

32:02.879 --> 32:03.797
I brought you here.

32:04.423 --> 32:06.174
Are you feeling better?

32:06.258 --> 32:07.426
The light's so bright.

32:15.642 --> 32:16.810
What's wrong now?

32:35.620 --> 32:37.080
What's wrong with me?

32:52.387 --> 32:54.598
What just happened?

32:54.681 --> 32:56.057
How is this possible?

32:56.141 --> 32:59.686
- What did I do to deserve--
- What is it? What's wrong?

33:04.399 --> 33:05.734
Yes, you.

33:05.817 --> 33:08.737
It's because of you.
This is all your fault!

33:08.820 --> 33:11.031
Why is it my fault again?

33:11.114 --> 33:13.158
Do you know what I went through
because of you?

33:13.241 --> 33:14.409
That's not the point!

33:14.493 --> 33:15.911
Then what is?

33:15.994 --> 33:17.162
I…

33:19.539 --> 33:20.707
I've become human.

33:22.334 --> 33:23.627
What?

33:23.710 --> 33:26.421
I've become human because of you!

33:30.008 --> 33:32.219
INN

33:40.936 --> 33:41.937
Where are you going?

33:43.230 --> 33:45.524
We should go our separate ways now.

33:46.233 --> 33:47.859
What about me then?

33:47.943 --> 33:49.402
What am I supposed to do?

33:51.863 --> 33:53.281
Move to a new place every day.

33:53.365 --> 33:54.533
What?

33:54.616 --> 33:56.952
Don't stay in one place for too long.

33:57.035 --> 33:59.788
That way, she'll have a harder time
finding your energy.

33:59.871 --> 34:00.997
Hey, wait!

34:03.708 --> 34:05.085
That's it?

34:05.168 --> 34:06.920
What if that fox finds me here?

34:07.003 --> 34:10.757
Maybe you're fine with dying,
but what about me?

34:10.840 --> 34:13.593
That's not really my problem.

34:25.689 --> 34:26.565
Calm down.

34:28.650 --> 34:30.443
Explain it so I can understand.

34:35.282 --> 34:36.992
I've become human.

34:37.617 --> 34:38.952
What more is there to explain?

34:39.661 --> 34:41.580
But is that really such a big deal?

34:42.872 --> 34:43.915
What?

34:43.999 --> 34:47.544
I mean, nine-tailed foxes eat
human livers to become human.

34:47.627 --> 34:49.546
At least, that's what the stories say.

34:50.338 --> 34:52.340
Are you out of your mind?

34:52.424 --> 34:57.429
If you were me, would you really choose
to lose your powers, grow old and sick,

34:57.512 --> 34:59.639
and die before even reaching a hundred?

34:59.723 --> 35:02.892
- You think I'd eat a liver just for that?
- All right.

35:03.393 --> 35:04.811
I get it.

35:05.645 --> 35:08.523
Then how did this happen?

35:08.607 --> 35:11.818
You wouldn't have suddenly
become human for no reason.

35:11.901 --> 35:13.153
That's…

35:14.988 --> 35:16.990
because I saved your life.

35:21.244 --> 35:23.580
As you were dying,
I was losing my spiritual power.

35:23.663 --> 35:27.542
So I saved you
just to stop that from happening.

35:28.752 --> 35:31.463
But how can they count that
as a good deed?

35:31.546 --> 35:33.131
How does that even add up?

35:33.214 --> 35:35.967
Do they have any idea
how many terrible things I've done?

35:36.593 --> 35:38.386
All because I saved one meager life?

35:42.265 --> 35:44.726
Well, I agree.

35:44.809 --> 35:46.561
You're not fit to be human yet.

35:46.645 --> 35:48.855
There must've been some mistake.

35:48.938 --> 35:50.899
You think so too, right?

35:52.776 --> 35:56.780
Anyway, since you became
human against your will,

35:56.863 --> 35:59.240
I really do feel for you.

36:02.494 --> 36:07.332
But there is something
I've been wanting to ask.

36:09.334 --> 36:10.627
What's that?

36:10.710 --> 36:14.881
When exactly will I go back
to how things were?

36:17.634 --> 36:18.551
What?

36:18.635 --> 36:20.929
You said so last night.

36:21.012 --> 36:24.057
That everything would be back
to normal by morning.

36:24.140 --> 36:25.934
And it's morning.

36:26.017 --> 36:28.853
Actually, it's already past morning.
It's lunchtime.

36:30.563 --> 36:31.690
When will it switch back?

36:34.818 --> 36:37.195
Have you even been listening to me?

36:38.446 --> 36:39.698
I'm human now.

36:40.782 --> 36:41.991
So?

36:42.075 --> 36:45.995
I'm human now, so how am I supposed
to turn things back the way they were?

36:48.039 --> 36:50.917
Wait, what are you talking about?

36:51.418 --> 36:52.293
No way.

36:52.377 --> 36:54.629
You're joking, aren't you?

36:56.005 --> 36:57.215
Does it look like I'm joking?

36:57.298 --> 37:00.009
This isn't a joke. This is hell.

37:00.093 --> 37:04.848
No, no. This can't be happening.
Please don't do this to me!

37:05.890 --> 37:08.685
Are you saying
I have to keep living like this?

37:09.936 --> 37:13.064
Yes, for the time being.

37:13.982 --> 37:15.400
"For the time being"?

37:15.483 --> 37:16.776
For how long?

37:18.445 --> 37:19.320
A few weeks?

37:19.946 --> 37:21.239
Well…

37:22.323 --> 37:23.199
A few months?

37:24.743 --> 37:26.369
Say something!

37:26.453 --> 37:29.789
What are you going to do?
There's no way I can live like this!

37:29.873 --> 37:31.541
Do you think I want to live like this?

37:31.624 --> 37:35.170
Then do something! Anything!

37:35.253 --> 37:36.963
There has to be a way, right?

37:37.046 --> 37:38.757
Do you even have to ask?

37:39.257 --> 37:41.509
If there isn't a way, I'll make one.

37:54.814 --> 37:57.650
Could you have gone any slower?
I said I was in a hurry.

37:58.318 --> 37:59.986
I'm sorry.

38:02.155 --> 38:03.156
I'm really sorry.

38:10.497 --> 38:12.457
That temper of yours, seriously.

38:14.667 --> 38:16.419
What are we doing here anyway?

38:16.503 --> 38:18.755
I have some things to say
and questions to ask.

38:19.464 --> 38:21.090
Something definitely went wrong.

38:29.349 --> 38:31.684
You there, could you leave for a moment?

38:31.768 --> 38:33.561
I have some business here.

38:33.645 --> 38:35.730
- Hey.
- What?

38:36.356 --> 38:37.857
He is

38:37.941 --> 38:39.818
no longer here.

38:40.902 --> 38:42.070
What?

38:42.153 --> 38:44.197
He left last night.

38:45.490 --> 38:47.659
That crazy old geezer!

38:49.953 --> 38:54.541
Since you've come all this way,
why don't you stay for some tea?

39:05.885 --> 39:07.262
Where did he go?

39:07.846 --> 39:09.389
I wouldn't know.

39:10.056 --> 39:14.310
How could a mere monk
fathom the divine will?

39:14.394 --> 39:17.146
There's something I need answers to.

39:18.147 --> 39:21.526
So I'd appreciate it if you could
just tell me where he went.

39:21.609 --> 39:23.903
He didn't say.

39:23.987 --> 39:28.116
But he told me to give you this.

39:30.535 --> 39:33.496
Since you'll be living
in the human world now,

39:34.163 --> 39:36.416
he said it's something
you'll definitely need.

39:47.927 --> 39:49.387
What is this?

39:49.470 --> 39:53.600
Your name is Ok-sun.
"Ok" for jade, and "Sun" for pure.

39:53.683 --> 39:58.187
Lord Pagun hoped
that choosing a name like this for you

39:58.688 --> 40:01.566
would help you rein in your temper.

40:01.649 --> 40:02.775
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD

40:11.367 --> 40:12.493
How did it go?

40:13.119 --> 40:14.495
Is there a way?

40:15.288 --> 40:17.665
Hey, say something.

40:19.042 --> 40:20.501
How did it go?

40:21.836 --> 40:23.296
STORAGE ROOM

40:27.258 --> 40:28.259
What are you doing?

40:29.636 --> 40:30.845
Hey.

40:33.890 --> 40:35.141
Carry this and follow me.

40:36.976 --> 40:38.186
What are these for?

40:39.854 --> 40:41.147
What are you doing?

40:43.149 --> 40:44.651
What is…

40:46.069 --> 40:48.029
Gosh, that smell! Are you crazy?

40:48.112 --> 40:49.572
Hey!

40:50.657 --> 40:52.617
I'm going to burn
this place to the ground!

40:52.700 --> 40:53.576
Jeez!

40:54.410 --> 40:56.579
Let me go!

40:56.663 --> 40:58.289
Excuse me, what's going on?

40:58.373 --> 41:00.333
Let me go!

41:00.959 --> 41:03.544
I'm going to burn this place down!

41:04.170 --> 41:06.297
I'm going to burn this place down!

41:06.381 --> 41:08.257
- What are you doing?
- Let me go!

41:09.634 --> 41:13.137
- Why are you doing this?
- Put me down!

41:15.473 --> 41:18.309
TRUSTED POLICE
WORKING WITH THE PEOPLE

41:22.355 --> 41:24.732
The head monk spoke up for you.

41:24.816 --> 41:27.193
He said you'd be able to
get out tomorrow morning.

41:27.276 --> 41:28.653
Tomorrow morning?

41:28.736 --> 41:31.447
Are you kidding me?
Tell them to let me out now.

41:31.531 --> 41:34.701
You're here for attempted arson.

41:34.784 --> 41:37.829
You should be grateful
they're letting you out tomorrow.

41:37.912 --> 41:40.331
Can't we just pay them off or something?

41:40.415 --> 41:41.874
Where would I get the money?

41:41.958 --> 41:43.418
I'm broke because of you.

41:43.501 --> 41:45.211
Whatever. This is pathetic.

41:45.294 --> 41:47.547
Good grief.

41:47.630 --> 41:49.549
Grab those two blankets over there.

41:49.632 --> 41:52.093
There won't be any left
when the drunks get here.

41:53.469 --> 41:55.847
By the way,
where's my wooden-handled dagger?

41:55.930 --> 41:57.015
What?

41:57.098 --> 41:58.558
The dagger I had.

41:59.308 --> 42:01.019
It was gone when I woke up.

42:02.478 --> 42:03.730
Don't tell me.

42:04.605 --> 42:06.315
Did you not bring it yesterday?

42:08.484 --> 42:10.194
Was there a dagger?

42:12.697 --> 42:14.198
Oh, that.

42:14.282 --> 42:16.325
I was all over the place yesterday.

42:17.535 --> 42:18.703
You left it behind?

42:18.786 --> 42:21.789
Yes. Was it important?

42:22.790 --> 42:24.167
Go and get it right now!

42:24.250 --> 42:25.376
Right now?

42:26.252 --> 42:28.046
You want me to go back there?

42:28.129 --> 42:30.757
Why? You want to wait until next year?

42:30.840 --> 42:32.633
That's not what I meant.

42:33.634 --> 42:38.139
After everything that happened yesterday,
how can I go back there alone this late?

42:38.222 --> 42:42.477
Let's just wait until morning
and go together, okay?

42:43.061 --> 42:46.939
It's the only Sajin Ritual Blade
left in the world.

42:47.565 --> 42:50.026
Sajin… what?

42:50.651 --> 42:53.571
It's a sacred dagger
that can sever and defy fate.

42:55.031 --> 42:57.366
If we want to get things back
to how they were…

42:58.743 --> 43:00.495
we might need it.

43:05.333 --> 43:06.751
Jeez.

43:23.059 --> 43:24.060
Is this the place?

43:24.685 --> 43:25.728
Yes.

43:26.604 --> 43:28.481
The NASDAQ is about to open.

43:28.564 --> 43:29.941
Where are we going at this hour?

43:30.024 --> 43:32.401
Jeez!

43:33.194 --> 43:34.529
What is this place?

43:34.612 --> 43:37.615
Where are we?
What are we looking for here?

43:39.325 --> 43:41.911
There's a lot of weird stuff in there,

43:42.537 --> 43:43.955
so don't be too shocked.

43:44.539 --> 43:46.332
Weird stuff like what?

43:47.083 --> 43:48.417
Hey, wait.

43:51.129 --> 43:52.880
Si-yeol!

43:53.881 --> 43:54.924
Damn it.

44:18.531 --> 44:19.824
Oh, jeez.

44:24.787 --> 44:27.790
Wait, why is it…

44:30.793 --> 44:34.338
What's wrong? What's supposed to be here?

44:34.964 --> 44:36.090
What is it?

44:36.716 --> 44:38.426
- There's nothing here, Beom.
- What?

44:42.638 --> 44:44.056
Seriously.

44:45.641 --> 44:47.435
It's just a construction site.

44:48.060 --> 44:51.022
You say there's something here?
Looks like there's nothing at all.

44:51.105 --> 44:53.232
Are you okay, Si-yeol?

44:54.775 --> 44:55.818
Yeah.

45:20.885 --> 45:22.553
Top teams

45:22.637 --> 45:26.265
from all over the world made offers.

45:31.103 --> 45:33.272
Stop it, Dad.

46:28.286 --> 46:30.454
Ms. Kim Ok-sun, you can come out now.

46:36.460 --> 46:38.004
Ms. Kim Ok-sun.

46:38.671 --> 46:40.131
I said, you can come out now.

46:48.097 --> 46:50.016
I told you yesterday.

46:50.099 --> 46:51.559
My name's not Kim Ok-sun.

46:52.268 --> 46:54.020
Then are you going to stay in here?

47:02.737 --> 47:04.739
I am coming out.

47:06.240 --> 47:08.242
But I'm not Kim Ok-sun.

47:43.903 --> 47:44.862
Hey.

47:46.072 --> 47:47.156
How can I help you?

47:47.239 --> 47:48.407
Call Kang Si-yeol for me.

47:49.200 --> 47:52.244
- I'm sorry, who?
- I just got released from here,

47:52.328 --> 47:54.997
but Si-yeol isn't here yet.
Tell him to get here fast.

47:57.625 --> 48:00.169
This isn't the place for jokes.
Please leave.

48:42.586 --> 48:43.629
Hey!

48:48.676 --> 48:50.094
Kang Si-yeol?

48:50.177 --> 48:52.304
I thought you'd abandoned me.

48:52.388 --> 48:54.557
What are you talking about?
Why would I do that?

48:54.640 --> 48:56.392
I need you more than ever right now.

48:56.475 --> 48:57.351
Really?

48:57.435 --> 48:59.311
Get in. We're going to Seoraksan Mountain.

48:59.395 --> 49:01.605
We have to hurry before it closes. Get in.

49:02.773 --> 49:03.816
Buckle up.

49:05.818 --> 49:08.696
- Hurry up. Come on.
- Okay.

49:09.947 --> 49:11.490
Okay, here we go.

49:12.825 --> 49:14.034
Let's go.

49:17.204 --> 49:19.248
Why Seoraksan Mountain all of a sudden?

49:19.331 --> 49:21.041
Do you think we have time for that?

49:21.125 --> 49:22.626
I found something.

49:22.710 --> 49:24.962
Right. Did you find
the wooden-handled dagger?

49:25.045 --> 49:29.216
No. When I got there,
there was nothing left.

49:29.300 --> 49:33.971
The dagger was gone,
and so was all the shaman stuff.

49:34.054 --> 49:35.097
What?

49:36.474 --> 49:38.767
Then what on earth did you find?

49:38.851 --> 49:40.186
Another

49:41.145 --> 49:42.605
nine-tailed fox.

49:43.564 --> 49:44.482
What?

49:48.152 --> 49:49.862
How long are we staying here?

49:49.945 --> 49:51.322
There's nothing there.

49:58.496 --> 50:01.290
COUPLE SAVED BY NINE-TAILED FOX
STARTS NEW LIFE THROUGH VOLUNTEERING

50:02.958 --> 50:04.835
That's absolute nonsense.

50:04.919 --> 50:07.838
There is no other nine-tailed fox
in this land besides me.

50:08.797 --> 50:10.216
How can you be so sure?

50:10.299 --> 50:11.592
I just am.

50:12.092 --> 50:15.346
If there were another being like me,
we would sense each other's energy.

50:15.429 --> 50:16.347
Even from a distance.

50:17.139 --> 50:18.724
Then what about those people?

50:19.266 --> 50:21.018
They're just talking nonsense.

50:21.101 --> 50:22.478
Humans are always like that.

50:22.561 --> 50:25.105
They either hallucinated
or just wanted attention.

50:26.106 --> 50:27.566
They didn't seem like that.

50:30.069 --> 50:31.153
How would you know?

50:32.905 --> 50:34.073
Because I met them myself.

50:35.741 --> 50:39.578
Gosh, I really thought
I was going to die that day.

50:40.746 --> 50:44.708
I think it was around 2 or 3 p.m.
when we entered Dinosaur Ridge.

50:45.584 --> 50:46.835
Sometime around then.

50:46.919 --> 50:50.798
But since it was winter,
the sun went down so fast.

50:50.881 --> 50:52.508
It was freezing cold,

50:52.591 --> 50:55.761
and we'd been hiking all day,
so we were exhausted.

50:55.844 --> 50:58.347
We couldn't see a thing in front of us.

50:58.430 --> 51:02.268
But she suddenly said
she was getting sleepy.

51:02.351 --> 51:04.853
It was because of hypothermia.

51:04.937 --> 51:08.065
If that happens on a mountain,
you're in big trouble.

51:08.148 --> 51:13.195
I forced her to stay awake
and was dragging her along

51:13.862 --> 51:16.156
when she suddenly appeared.

51:19.410 --> 51:22.121
She was a very pretty young lady.

51:22.204 --> 51:26.584
She suddenly appeared and asked,
"Would you like some help?"

51:27.251 --> 51:29.587
We thought we were seeing things.

51:29.670 --> 51:34.592
So we asked who she was
and if she was a ghost.

51:35.259 --> 51:39.763
She said she was a fox trying
to become human by doing good deeds.

51:39.847 --> 51:44.101
Anyway, she lit a fire for us
and helped us find our way.

51:44.184 --> 51:46.604
So, thankfully, we made it back alive.

51:47.605 --> 51:49.273
She said she was a fox, right?

51:49.356 --> 51:51.233
The young woman said that herself?

51:51.734 --> 51:54.612
I understand if you don't believe us.

51:54.695 --> 51:56.739
But it's true.

51:56.822 --> 51:59.074
Actually, there are
a few others besides us.

52:00.367 --> 52:01.243
A few others?

52:01.869 --> 52:03.370
After the article came out,

52:03.454 --> 52:06.707
a lot of people got in touch,
not just you.

52:06.790 --> 52:10.419
They all said they were saved
by that young lady on Seoraksan Mountain.

52:13.547 --> 52:14.632
By the way,

52:14.715 --> 52:16.925
you said there was nothing there, right?

52:17.009 --> 52:18.135
What?

52:18.218 --> 52:22.056
You said there were no shamanic items
and no Sajin Ritual Blade either.

52:22.139 --> 52:23.223
Oh, that.

52:23.807 --> 52:26.226
It was spotless,
as if someone had swept it clean.

52:26.310 --> 52:28.979
Who could have cleaned the place up
overnight like that?

52:29.730 --> 52:31.982
Maybe those guys came and went last night.

52:32.066 --> 52:33.233
Not likely.

52:33.984 --> 52:36.111
They wouldn't know that I've become human.

52:36.195 --> 52:38.447
Why would they risk going back there?

52:38.530 --> 52:40.074
And how could they have known

52:40.157 --> 52:42.701
that you were stupid enough
to leave the dagger?

52:42.785 --> 52:44.161
Hey!

52:44.244 --> 52:46.121
Come on, that's not the point.

52:47.247 --> 52:49.625
What do you think
about what I said earlier?

52:49.708 --> 52:53.712
If we find that fox on the mountain,
couldn't she turn things back to normal?

52:54.463 --> 52:55.923
Don't you think it's strange?

52:56.006 --> 52:57.091
What is?

52:57.174 --> 53:00.219
A deserted construction site wiped clean,

53:00.302 --> 53:02.763
and a newspaper scrap
about a nine-tailed fox

53:02.846 --> 53:05.683
lying around
as if it were deliberately left there.

53:05.766 --> 53:08.143
I guess…

53:09.937 --> 53:10.813
Take it out.

53:12.564 --> 53:14.066
Sure.

53:20.364 --> 53:22.282
COUPLE SAVED BY NINE-TAILED FOX…

53:22.366 --> 53:23.701
SUNDAY, NOVEMBER 16, 1997

53:25.577 --> 53:27.996
See? I knew it.

53:28.747 --> 53:29.832
What?

53:30.332 --> 53:31.291
Look at the date.

53:31.375 --> 53:32.292
NOVEMBER 16, 1997

53:32.376 --> 53:34.086
This newspaper is over 20 years old.

53:34.169 --> 53:36.880
Isn't this a bit too convenient
to be a coincidence?

53:37.423 --> 53:39.883
Someone is pulling the strings here.

53:39.967 --> 53:41.343
Who?

53:43.178 --> 53:44.930
Probably those guys up there.

53:46.181 --> 53:48.267
That's just how deities treat humans.

53:48.350 --> 53:51.729
Under the pretext of things like
fate or coincidence,

53:51.812 --> 53:53.605
they manipulate humans however they want.

53:54.523 --> 53:58.861
So there's no nine-tailed fox
on Seoraksan Mountain?

54:00.154 --> 54:01.405
I wouldn't know.

54:01.488 --> 54:05.367
Whether there's an actual nine-tailed fox
and they're sending us there,

54:06.118 --> 54:08.036
or if there's another reason for this.

54:09.121 --> 54:10.038
Let's go.

54:10.122 --> 54:13.876
I need to see for myself
what they're up to.

54:41.278 --> 54:42.321
Is that Park Bi-ryong?

54:44.031 --> 54:45.491
How nice.

54:48.118 --> 54:49.244
Do you know this bear?

54:56.752 --> 54:59.129
The sun will be setting soon.

55:00.297 --> 55:03.926
Wouldn't it be better to sleep nearby
and hike up tomorrow?

55:04.009 --> 55:06.136
We're trying to get stranded anyway.

55:07.638 --> 55:10.057
But aren't we a little unprepared?

55:10.140 --> 55:12.142
You do have a plan, right?

55:14.436 --> 55:18.065
It's just one night on a mountain.
Why are you making such a fuss?

55:18.148 --> 55:19.608
Have you forgotten who I am?

55:19.691 --> 55:21.568
I lived on a mountain for centuries.

55:23.028 --> 55:24.279
Just follow me.

55:31.662 --> 55:32.621
Wait for me.

55:44.216 --> 55:45.509
Are you all right?

55:46.301 --> 55:48.971
Go. Just keep going.

55:54.560 --> 55:58.897
Eat this and hang in there.
You're still so young.

56:04.236 --> 56:07.573
Just how much steeper does this get?

56:08.282 --> 56:11.159
This useless human body.

56:28.594 --> 56:29.970
Hey, young man!

56:31.013 --> 56:32.931
- Take these with you.
- Pardon?

56:34.182 --> 56:36.768
- No, I'm okay.
- Just take them with you.

56:37.394 --> 56:38.478
And also…

56:41.982 --> 56:43.400
Here, take this.

56:45.736 --> 56:47.529
If you give all of this to me…

56:47.613 --> 56:48.822
It's fine.

56:50.407 --> 56:51.533
But…

56:54.202 --> 56:56.330
What's wrong with humans today?

56:57.289 --> 56:58.707
They keep giving us things,

56:58.790 --> 57:01.418
looking at us with teary eyes,
and holding our hands.

57:02.252 --> 57:04.004
Do we look that pathetic?

57:07.799 --> 57:08.675
Excuse me!

57:10.636 --> 57:11.595
Hold on a second.

57:14.598 --> 57:16.600
Yes? How can I help you?

57:17.225 --> 57:18.185
We received a report.

57:22.689 --> 57:24.566
I'm telling you, it's not like that.

57:24.650 --> 57:26.818
Who said anyone was going to die?

57:27.361 --> 57:29.279
- Jeez.
- Are you sure?

57:29.363 --> 57:32.783
If you weren't thinking such things,

57:32.866 --> 57:35.410
why would you climb the mountain
at this hour dressed like that?

57:35.494 --> 57:37.746
We've received several reports.

57:37.829 --> 57:40.123
I don't know what you're going through,

57:40.207 --> 57:42.334
but you're a young couple
with a future ahead of you.

57:42.417 --> 57:43.502
Please think it over.

57:43.585 --> 57:45.003
- No--
- We're not a couple.

57:45.087 --> 57:47.422
And we're not here to die,
so just let us go.

57:48.423 --> 57:52.344
We were dragged down for nothing.
How are we supposed to get back up?

57:52.427 --> 57:53.845
You're going back up?

57:53.929 --> 57:56.640
Of course I am.
Why else would I have come this far?

57:56.723 --> 57:59.726
Goodness, you have no idea
how dangerous mountains are.

57:59.810 --> 58:03.313
Anyway, you can't go up now.
You can't see anything, and it's cold.

58:03.397 --> 58:08.026
Even expert hikers would be
in serious trouble without proper gear.

58:12.155 --> 58:15.617
MULLEBOGO RESTAURANT

58:17.911 --> 58:19.162
Oh man.

58:19.246 --> 58:20.372
Jeez.

58:20.455 --> 58:22.416
My goodness.

58:25.168 --> 58:27.879
I thought you lived
on a mountain for centuries.

58:28.714 --> 58:30.340
I've realized one thing for sure.

58:30.966 --> 58:32.300
I'd rather die

58:32.384 --> 58:34.553
than live as a human.

58:41.601 --> 58:44.604
It's all cooked,
so you can eat it right away.

58:44.688 --> 58:45.564
Enjoy your meal.

58:45.647 --> 58:46.940
- Thank you for the meal.
- Sure.

59:00.704 --> 59:03.582
Gosh, you're spilling everywhere.

59:05.459 --> 59:08.336
You hiked with your legs,
so why are your arms shaking?

59:09.337 --> 59:10.714
How should I know?

59:11.256 --> 59:14.092
There's not one part of my body
that doesn't hurt.

59:16.970 --> 59:18.597
Okay.

59:31.359 --> 59:32.360
Here.

59:33.695 --> 59:34.988
Say "ah."

59:45.999 --> 59:47.292
Is it good?

59:48.668 --> 59:51.338
Give me some more.
And some broth too. It's a bit dry.

59:56.968 --> 59:58.011
Here.

01:00:03.975 --> 01:00:05.352
Careful, it's hot.

01:00:08.480 --> 01:00:09.773
You've got quite an appetite.

01:00:10.690 --> 01:00:11.817
You want this?

01:00:12.317 --> 01:00:13.735
Yes, the chives too.

01:00:15.195 --> 01:00:17.405
- Please come again.
- Thank you.

01:00:23.620 --> 01:00:24.830
Are you asleep already?

01:00:25.372 --> 01:00:26.623
Jeez.

01:00:34.381 --> 01:00:35.924
She must've been really tired.

01:01:11.710 --> 01:01:14.629
Man, what on earth am I thinking?

01:01:17.090 --> 01:01:18.049
Hey, wake up.

01:01:18.717 --> 01:01:21.303
Come on, wake up.

01:01:27.058 --> 01:01:28.602
What's this?

01:01:29.102 --> 01:01:31.396
Why am I suddenly…

01:02:08.850 --> 01:02:10.727
SPECIAL APPEARANCE BY SON SUK

01:02:35.043 --> 01:02:37.921
NO TAIL TO TELL

01:02:38.004 --> 01:02:39.589
Did you have a weird dream or something?

01:02:39.673 --> 01:02:41.967
It wasn't a dream.
It was more like a prophecy…

01:02:42.509 --> 01:02:45.679
You seem to keep forgetting,
but you're just a human woman now.

01:02:47.639 --> 01:02:50.475
I get it. This is like hitting
on a female. It's called flirting.

01:02:50.558 --> 01:02:51.434
Are you nuts?

01:02:51.518 --> 01:02:53.979
Look into the records of the car accident
from nine years ago.

01:02:54.062 --> 01:02:57.399
Find out everything
about where he lives and what he's doing.

01:02:57.482 --> 01:02:59.234
You can't just do this all of a sudden.

01:02:59.317 --> 01:03:00.944
How can you do this?

01:03:01.027 --> 01:03:02.946
Have you ever seen
any other nine-tailed foxes?

01:03:03.029 --> 01:03:05.115
- I have.
- Are you okay?

01:03:05.198 --> 01:03:06.574
Do you need help?

01:03:10.203 --> 01:03:11.288
Geum-ho?

01:03:12.706 --> 01:03:14.708
Subtitle translation by Susanna Kim
